  "notes": "# Goro 0.5.0-alpha.2\n\nThis experimental prerelease replaces CodeMirror with Monaco. The existing Goro\npalettes, document safety and Go tooling workflows are retained.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Per-file Monaco models preserve undo history and view state across tabs.\n- Completion follows exact unsaved buffers, refreshes as prefixes grow and stays\n  active in snippet placeholders. Stale requests cannot overwrite current results.\n- Autosave writes drafts without waiting for formatting. Explicit Save preserves\n  incomplete Go when gopls reports a parser error; Run still flushes pending saves.\n- Local syntax errors appear on their source rows. Operational failures appear in\n  the status bar and Problems dock instead of covering the editor.\n- Optional Vim motions, context mappings and Insert-mode preferences are available\n  in Settings. Markdown rows render sanitized previews and expose source on hover\n  or selection.\n- Settings use switches; controls have restrained hover, press and focus feedback.\n  Goro Dark/Light retain the existing stored theme IDs and palettes.\n- Windows start centered at 1200 × 720 without maximizing.\n\n## Acceptance and limits\n\nThe maintainer reported successful manual testing of the dev application on\n2026-10-05. Source CI and package verification must pass for the final release\ncommit before publication; this document is preparation, not proof of publication.\n\nClean-machine installation, signed upgrades, complete native interaction coverage,\nIME/accessibility and measured editor performance remain open. Complex Markdown\nlayouts and Unix descendant containment also need further acceptance. This alpha\ndoes not establish beta or production readiness.\n\nSee [release readiness](../RELEASE_READINESS.md) and [editor behavior](../EDITOR.md).\n",
